# Files that bash, shellcheck, grep or the installer read byte for byte must stay LF, also in a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' default). With CRLF, shellcheck reports
# SC1017 on every line, and a CR ends up inside patterns, branch names and file names the scripts compare.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.env     text eol=lf
*.append  text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
